erpersonal (nasty remarks) and memory for numbers (attention). Could be problematic for crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, but difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence. Concerns: communication, teamwork, development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Concerns: temperament, attitude.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely candidate B has strong reliability and stress, but interpersonal issues (nasty remarks) could be severe for crew cooperation. Candidate C has good decision and calm but communication issues and egocentric. Candidate D has responsibility but hot temper and know-it-all. Candidate A has leadership but show-off and not open.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate B: reliability and stress handling are crucial, but nasty remarks could be mitigated? However, crew cooperation is essential. Candidate C's communication difficulty is also big. Candidate D's hot temper is serious. Candidate A's attitude also concerning.\n\nMaybe B is still best because conscientiousness and stress handling outweigh interpersonal remarks? But \"makes nasty remarks about his colleagues\" is a serious crew cooperation issue. Could be disqualifying.\n\nCandidate C: calm, correct decisions, technical, but egocentric and poor communication. That also harms crew.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility, concentration, problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all could affect crew.\n\nAll have issues. Need to decide which has least severe concerns relative to strengths. B's nasty remarks is a direct interpersonal problem. D's hot temper also interpersonal. A's show-off and not open to ideas also interpersonal. C's egocentric and communication difficulty also interpersonal.\n\nWhich candidate has strongest overall? Perhaps B's strengths (conscientious, stress, weather, computer) are highly relevant for long-distance flights. Interpersonal issue could be addressed with training. Others have more severe technical gaps? C has good technical but communication issues. D has good problem solving but temperament.\n\nI think B is leading. So I will state recommendation for Candidate B, citing strengths and acknowledging concern.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
